WEBVTT

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.140
She's not here! There's 
no Hato-kun here!

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:12.950
Huh?

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:17.270
She hasn't been to the club 
room for a while, either?

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:20.150
There's more to this, isn't there?

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:22.120
Something had to have happened.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.440
No, no, no, that's all. Seriously.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.760
Basically, I quit my job,

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.700
and Hato-kun was worried, 
and that's all.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:32.810
Was your quitting that 
big a deal for her?

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:34.090
But why?

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:36.470
Those are the eyes of a liar!

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:39.060
It's true! I'm as shocked as you are!

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.630
Call. Ask Hato.

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:47.500
No. If she isn't coming, it's 
because she doesn't want to come.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:50.730
And it'd be weird to ask why now, 
and even moreso on the phone...

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:51.690
Ask.

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:05.960
Connecting you to voice mail...

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:11.550
<b><i>Genshiken Second Generation</i></b>

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:24.270
She...

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:27.370
She realized!

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:29.860
She realized, and that's why she ran.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:32.840
She ran from you too, huh?

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:35.240
This is a huge honking deal!

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:37.980
You just wanted to say "honking."

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:42.940
I guess the obvious idea is that 
having Rame-sempai at home all day

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:46.030
means she doesn't want 
to change there anymore.

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:47.080
I don't know about that--

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:50.980
But refusing to expect the obvious

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:52.880
is what makes us rotten girls!

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:56.090
I prefer to think that Hato-kun

00:01:56.090 --> 00:02:00.980
is torn between not wanting to change while 
sempai's around, and wanting him to see!

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:02.350
I'm sure you would.

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:09.710
So basically, she's coming to university,
 but doesn't want to see us or Madarame-san.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:16.740
Time for the second ever,

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.780
"I can't believe we're 
actually going on a trip!"

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.370
Waiting in the Club Room.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:36.400
Sorry.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.420
I don't know if a graduate 
should really be here.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:41.320
No, no, we're glad you came.

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:44.920
We were worried about having Kuchiki-sempai 
and Hato-kun alone together.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:47.640
I prefer Kuchi x Mata!

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:48.770
Ow...

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:50.530
Let's go to the roof.

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:53.010
I haven't felt this 
angry in a long time.

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:55.640
Hato's late. Is she coming?

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:57.680
She can't back out!

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:00.110
She told Sue she'd go, right?

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:07.520
She's here!

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:08.880
Over here!

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:11.170
She looks different than usual today.

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:22.310
Hello, everyone.

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:23.590
I'm sorry.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:31.730
We've done this before...

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:35.270
Gone on a trip with all of Genshiken.

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:38.230
Not Yamanashi, but to Karuizawa.

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:40.450
Is it something you do every year?

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:43.630
No, it's not.

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:46.700
Sasahara-san's little 
sister was here then,

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:49.120
and it was just something we did.

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:56.290
It's a mystery how Sue knew about 
our trip to Karuizawa, though.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:59.730
"I can't believe we're 
all going on a trip!"

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:01.420
What doesn't kill us makes us crippled!

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:02.970
That's not what we want.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:04.050
I'm in despair!

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:04.980
What?

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:06.760
All's well that end's well!

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.140
I don't really get it.

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:11.310
But you want us to help 
out Hato-kun on this trip?

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:15.480
But I can't go with a guy...

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:18.000
What is that?

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.010
What, Ohgi-sempai?

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:23.980
No, I mean... how do 
we contact Hato-kun?

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:26.160
Her phone! She's not 
picking up her phone!

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:27.950
1 1 5!

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:30.290
A telegram, you mean!

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:32.210
A telegram?

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:34.250
It's cheap.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:36.650
25 characters is 440 yen.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:39.880
Um... "Genshiken Trip."

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.940
Come along.

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:43.490
Without punctuation, that's 25 exactly.

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:45.080
I'll send it.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:46.680
Um... couldn't we just send a text--

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:48.070
Is it a celebratory telegram?

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:49.460
Why?

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:51.180
There's all different kinds!

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.390
Why are you taking pictures?

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:56.600
The sky of Tachikawa!

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.520
The clocks of Tachikawa!

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.690
The sign saying "Tachikawa" 
of Tachikawa!

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:03.240
Us in Tachikawa!

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:07.980
I was surprised too.
 I'd never gotten a telegram.

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:09.910
And it came with a stuffed bear.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:13.530
I told them a text message 
would work just as well.

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:20.840
Express Train #101 is 
now arriving on track 6.

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:22.500
Backlighting means victory! {From the manga "Perfect Superman".}

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:50.160
<b>A Tour of the Takeda Clan's History</b>

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:50.160
Look at this, everyone!

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:52.910
The coolest guy in the civil wars was 
Shingen, and the best general was Shingen,

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:54.900
and the coolest guy in Kai was Shingen!

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:58.150
I count myself as the twenty-fifth 
of Takeda's twenty-four generals,

00:05:58.150 --> 00:06:00.980
and I've taken the liberty of 
detailing his glorious deeds.

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:02.450
I don't really care.

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:04.760
No. Not okay. As a Japanese person--

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:07.010
No, as a human being, that's not okay!

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:08.770
What the heck?

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:10.970
You decided where we're going 
without asking us, either.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:12.410
What are you saying?

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:14.560
You guys weren't settling on anything.

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:15.780
He's bald with a beard!

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:17.940
He is! And he's still a bottom!

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:18.980
Seriously?

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:20.370
It's the low overcoming the high!  {An obscure term from the civil wars.}

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:23.220
Saigou Takamori was also 
supposed to be bald and fat.

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:23.650
What?

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:26.520
I'm sorry, can anybody 
who's not gay leave?

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:29.120
It's said that a hero 
enjoys his lusts, but...

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:33.080
What kind of lusts do 
you think they enjoyed?

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:35.110
In Shingen's case,

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:39.540
he wrote regretful letters to his 
younger darlings, so he's the real thing!

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:42.750
It was normal back then, though.

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:45.450
And he was supposedly 
very weak and ill too.

00:06:45.450 --> 00:06:47.730
How great, huh?

00:06:47.730 --> 00:06:50.050
By the way, my personal favorite story

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:51.900
is the fight between 
his successor Katsuyori

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:55.140
<b>Takeda Shrine</b>

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:55.140
and the retainers who served Shingen.

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:57.480
A love triangle over a great general

00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:00.530
that continues even after his death!

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:01.730
It's great!

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:03.190
Thank you, civil wars!

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:05.260
Thank you, Takeda Clan!

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:06.230
<b>Isawa Hot Springs Station</b>

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:07.850
Yoshi Warriors.  {Pun on samurai warriors, a video game.}

00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:10.580
I'm getting a glimpse into 
the potential of history.

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:12.680
I've heard enough about history for now.

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:15.380
And so for you, Yajimacchi, 
we've got the Isawa Hot Springs.

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:16.550
For me?

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:20.710
It's a new onsen! It appeared in a 
field sometime about 70 years ago.

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:23.050
I can tell you its history if you want.

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:23.990
Please don't!

00:07:23.990 --> 00:07:26.220
Let's get to the inn for now.

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:28.260
We've walked so much.

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:33.490
This inn's pretty nice.

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:35.920
I see. I see.

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:37.850
You think they get TV here?

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:39.770
I've prepared for if they don't!

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:42.120
I can record at my house and send 
it over wi-fi and the Internet!

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:45.200
We can enjoy our shows in real 
time at the end of the Earth!

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:45.940
Huh?

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:47.300
There's no Internet here.

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:49.750
No!

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:51.870
Come on in, Hato-kun.

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:52.990
Right.

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:56.730
They've got some snacks.

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:58.170
I'll make tea.

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:00.990
Yeah? Thanks.

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:04.050
What are these called again?

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:07.270
Whenever I see one, I feel 
like I'm on vacation.

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:09.840
That's called a kyousoku.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:12.850
I see. Kyousoku, kyousoku...

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:16.040
Anyway, I guess one of 
the perks of unemployment

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:17.760
is getting to take a 
vacation on a weekday.

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:26.260
Hey, where are you getting 
a job, Kuchiki-kun?

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:28.580
My dad's getting me a job at a bank.

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:30.450
Oh. Nice.

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:33.200
Seriously! Is there any point 
to all those rules about bowing?

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:35.700
And why do they insist on me 
not saying "nyo" all the time?

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:39.520
How deeply you bow signifies how you 
feel and what you're saying, right?

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:41.330
Ninety degrees is the most polite.

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:44.380
And don't clasp your hands behind your 
back, keep them clasped in front.

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:45.540
You're a slave of society!

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:48.150
Former slave. Now I'm a NEET.

00:08:48.150 --> 00:08:49.460
Um, what are you--

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:51.260
Charge into the boy's room next door!

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:52.970
Yay! Hello, folks!

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:54.090
Excuse us.

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:55.900
This is a nice room.

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:58.180
It's just you three guys, 
so it feels pretty big.

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:01.240
You can see the mountains 
from here, can't you?

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:03.290
Girls love checking out people's rooms.

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:05.910
We do, yeah.

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:09.300
I enjoyed seeing your room, Rame-sempai.

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:10.280
Seriously?

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:11.270
You're awful.

00:09:11.270 --> 00:09:15.210
My first time visiting a guy's 
room was Madarame-sempai's place.

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:16.040
Really?

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:18.090
I went to an all girls high school.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:20.740
So I didn't have many 
chances. Or any, actually.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:23.090
I'm amazed your parents 
let you come here.

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:25.330
Did you tell them there 
were guys going too?

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:27.570
The magic words were "school trip."

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:30.210
My sister's away from home 
all the time on them.

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:30.930
I see.

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:33.820
Her trips are real school trips, right?

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:35.700
But in our case...

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:38.320
No, no, no, don't underestimate 
us humanities types.

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:40.540
You won't be getting any sleep tonight!

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:41.540
Yeah.

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:43.450
We've got a lot to talk about.

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:46.140
Oh, Hato-chin. What will 
you be doing for your bath?

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:49.060
What are you talking about?  
Hato's going to the guy's bath.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:51.150
Oh, no, Yajimacchi.

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:53.820
I was asking if she'd take 
it before or after dinner.

00:09:54.450 --> 00:09:56.240
W-Well...

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:57.650
Before, right?

00:09:57.650 --> 00:10:01.100
The baths here are supposed 
to be really nice.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:04.430
They've got waterfalls, herbal 
baths, and open-air baths.

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:06.120
I can't wait, can you?

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:07.250
No...

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:09.210
I'll use the one in my room.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:10.700
Why?

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:11.630
"Why?"

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:12.610
Don't force him.

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:15.920
We're at a hot springs! The bath 
in your room isn't a hot springs!

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:17.510
But Hato's got--

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:20.040
Got?

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:21.330
Nothing...

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:23.810
Hato, you decide.

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:26.260
What do we do?

00:10:26.260 --> 00:10:27.270
Want to go?

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:28.970
We'll do the mixed bath!

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:30.760
Just like in Karuizawa!

00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:34.330
Guys and girls go in at different 
times! Don't be weird!

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:35.870
Let's go! Let's go!

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:37.860
They've got towels and stuff over there.

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:40.110
Yeah. I guess I might 
as well, since we're here.

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:44.580
Hato-kun.

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:46.380
Yes?

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:49.000
I recommend it too.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.040
The hot springs.

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.010
Enough!

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:05.970
That's a misdemeanor.

00:11:06.210 --> 00:11:09.240
I can't see a thing. This is rough.

00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:11.860
It's not rough. Go 
take off your glasses.

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:14.190
Normally it's the guys who do this.

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:16.560
You're worried too, right Ohno-sempai?

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:19.450
Beautiful Hato-chin is 
all alone with the guys.

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:20.530
And totally smooth!

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:21.360
You--

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:24.570
The fantasy train in my 
mind is out of control!

00:11:24.570 --> 00:11:27.170
We don't even know if 
they're over there!

00:11:27.170 --> 00:11:28.550
They might be using the bath in the room.

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:30.310
No way.

00:11:30.310 --> 00:11:33.720
Ohgi-sempai's on it, 
and Sue-san's helping!

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:35.630
Together, those two are invincible.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:37.310
Invincible?

00:11:37.310 --> 00:11:39.420
What are you fighting against?

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:43.850
After that happened, we started to 
understand each other a little better.

00:11:43.850 --> 00:11:45.970
Or maybe you could say 
they understood me better.

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:48.360
I was imagining BL

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:50.480
between you and Madarame-san.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:55.330
I've drawn... dozens of 
pictures already...

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:58.750
I guess I stopped running.

00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:01.640
I'm glad I was able to change.

00:12:03.390 --> 00:12:06.240
Glad you were able to change?

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:09.080
Yes.

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:13.370
I'm going to take a bath too.

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:14.710
Um...

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:21.630
Why was it a good thing 
that you could change?

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:24.230
Hato-kun,

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:26.600
do you regret being here right now?

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:30.110
I don't, but...

00:12:30.110 --> 00:12:32.610
Then isn't that enough?

00:12:48.820 --> 00:12:52.170
I'll seduce Hato-chin 
with my Sukikiyo pose! {Character from an obscure fighting game.}

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:53.790
I can't wait!

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:04.170
Hato-chin!

00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:21.110
KO Count: 1.

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:23.740
Sue's not here, huh?

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:26.930
In America, sometimes 
you just take a shower.

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:28.970
Maybe she doesn't like hot springs.

00:13:28.970 --> 00:13:30.390
I don't think so...

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:32.010
I'm sorry I'm late.

00:13:32.010 --> 00:13:34.400
Did you get to talk to Hato-kun?

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:39.310
Yes, I did. A little.

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:46.800
What's that laugh?

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:48.940
I was just thinking about how happy I feel.

00:13:49.190 --> 00:13:51.570
I mean, isn't this wonderful?

00:13:51.570 --> 00:13:54.500
Trips! Friends! Open baths!

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:57.940
What? You had me thinking 
you'd gotten engaged.

00:13:57.940 --> 00:13:59.500
Wait, Ohno-sempai.

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:02.790
Your breasts were that big before 
you began seeing Tanaka-sempai?

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:05.670
What? Yes, I guess...

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:11.240
Ohhh... and even after seeing Sasa-sempai, your 
breasts are still like that, Ohgi-sempai?

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:15.200
There's no good answer to that question.

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:19.120
Looks like it's just an 
urban legend, Yajimacchi.

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:20.090
What is?

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:23.010
You're not gonna say, "Do 
you want to touch them?"

00:14:23.010 --> 00:14:24.380
Not this time.

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:26.700
The freshmen might freak out...

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:30.590
After all we've been through?
  I bet Yoshitake-san would love it.

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:32.930
They say if you rub 
them they get bigger!

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:33.690
She's already rubbing Yajima-san's.

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:34.590
I'm just fat!

00:14:34.590 --> 00:14:35.850
Oh come on, it can't hurt!

00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:35.850
Shut up!

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:38.890
Bouncy boobs! Damn it!

00:14:39.840 --> 00:14:42.290
Hey, Sue! Be quiet!

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:52.100
Thanks.

00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:53.490
No problem.

00:15:07.580 --> 00:15:09.800
It's nice to have a big bath.

00:15:10.940 --> 00:15:12.990
Y-Yeah.

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:18.980
So smooth... that's not a guy's skin.

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:21.100
Whoops.

00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:34.040
I never thought I'd go to a hot 
springs and go, "Ooh," and, "Aah."

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:38.020
I've even got a hot springs episode 
folder on my hard drive too.

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:39.230
Hot springs episode?

00:15:39.230 --> 00:15:43.180
Yeah. You know, just downloading 
the good pics from the Internet...

00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:45.820
Haven't done it lately, though.

00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:50.580
But now that I'm not working, I'm 
going to have more time on my hands.

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:52.670
I can spend as much time 
on the Internet as I want.

00:15:52.670 --> 00:15:53.600
Um...

00:15:55.210 --> 00:15:58.720
What are you going to do now?

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:02.180
No, I'm sorry.

00:16:02.180 --> 00:16:05.020
That's not what I mean... 
What I mean is...

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:10.200
I'll look for a job.

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:14.410
I only took the one I had 
because it was near campus.

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:16.910
I'm going to be more careful next time.

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:18.050
Okay...

00:16:18.050 --> 00:16:21.900
It feels like I'm just now graduating.

00:16:25.850 --> 00:16:26.910
Sempai.

00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:28.460
Y-Yeah?

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:30.520
Thank you for everything.

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:35.310
I've apologized a lot, and 
said a lot of rude things,

00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:38.150
but I don't think I've ever thanked you.

00:16:38.150 --> 00:16:40.570
Well...

00:16:40.570 --> 00:16:45.400
For a second there, I thought you were going to 
stop coming to my place and stop cross-dressing.

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:47.690
But just for a second.

00:16:48.700 --> 00:16:50.540
Are you?

00:16:50.540 --> 00:16:52.510
Well...

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:55.340
You're really stopping?

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:57.010
I don't know.

00:16:57.010 --> 00:17:01.200
But I think I'll have to at some point.

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:02.000
Why?

00:17:04.970 --> 00:17:07.980
Because, well...

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:10.170
A lot's going to change.

00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:13.410
It has to change...

00:17:13.870 --> 00:17:16.410
Me, and everyone around me.

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:19.180
I mean you quit your job--

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:23.580
I can't say there was some 
big motivation behind it.

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:27.730
I just kind of went with the flow, 
and this is how it turned out.

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:29.110
Went with the flow?

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:33.840
I figure cross-dressing's just 
like robots, lolis, trains, or BL.

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:36.480
It's just something you're into.

00:17:36.480 --> 00:17:38.030
So don't worry, Hato-kun.

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:40.300
You're an otaku.

00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:43.410
That will never change.

00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:49.420
And that means whether or not you 
cross-dress isn't really that important.

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:53.960
Do it if you want,

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:56.330
and stop when you want to stop.

00:17:56.330 --> 00:17:59.260
And then you can decide 
if you'll start again.

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:02.740
Doesn't thinking that way make things easier?

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:03.600
I can decide?

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:04.270
Yup, yup.

00:18:04.510 --> 00:18:06.730
You've still got plenty of time.

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:16.110
Yeah.

00:18:25.050 --> 00:18:26.440
And then all of a sudden,

00:18:26.440 --> 00:18:28.860
I was enveloped by a white shadow.

00:18:28.860 --> 00:18:31.420
And the next thing I knew, 
I woke up in my futon!

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:33.590
I'm not saying it was aliens, 
but it was aliens!

00:18:33.590 --> 00:18:36.860
Do you want me to dissect you?

00:18:36.860 --> 00:18:38.170
No, sir.

00:18:38.170 --> 00:18:40.470
So before our toast,

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:44.990
let's start our first, "Should Hato-chan 
dress as a boy or girl?" meeting!

00:18:44.990 --> 00:18:46.680
I say girl!

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:49.410
We're all having dinner in our yukata.

00:18:49.890 --> 00:18:51.600
From all that stuff you brought,

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:54.570
you've got the tools you need, don't you?

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:59.150
I want to see Hato-kun looking cute!

00:18:59.150 --> 00:19:00.000
No, wait--

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:02.390
Who thinks Hato-chan 
should dress as a girl!

00:19:03.840 --> 00:19:05.120
I guess I'm in.

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:10.710
All right.

00:19:13.310 --> 00:19:15.300
This is...

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:18.630
...kind of embarrassing, 
when I think about it.

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:22.160
No, I think you do look 
more natural this way.

00:19:22.160 --> 00:19:24.560
Yajimacchi's given her approval!

00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:26.630
I don't mean that it's okay to cross-dress!

00:19:26.630 --> 00:19:28.790
I just mean that I'm more used 
to it! Don't get the wrong idea.

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:30.520
I know that!

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:32.950
You're a real tsundere, after all.

00:19:32.950 --> 00:19:34.780
Who calls people tsundere anymore?

00:19:37.010 --> 00:19:38.470
Am I saying it?

00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:38.910
Yeah.

00:19:38.910 --> 00:19:40.450
You're the president.

00:19:41.480 --> 00:19:44.530
Um... okay, then.

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:46.450
Cheers!

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:48.290
Cheers!

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:54.770
Then we can add King 
Arthur and Lancelot!

00:19:54.770 --> 00:19:57.670
Add Caesar, 'cause he's bald too!

00:19:57.670 --> 00:19:59.690
That'll make it all old men.

00:19:59.690 --> 00:20:00.720
Not that I mind...

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:02.940
We can add young Japanese boys 
like Ushiwakamaru and Ranmaru,

00:20:02.940 --> 00:20:05.550
and give it some shota too!

00:20:05.550 --> 00:20:07.890
That's way too many characters!

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:08.800
Is it?

00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:12.120
I think a school for reincarnated heroes 
is perfect for a collaborative work.

00:20:12.120 --> 00:20:15.330
But who's going to figure 
out a plot for it?

00:20:15.330 --> 00:20:16.960
It's just a buncha jokes.

00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:19.450
No problem. We steal from Femto.

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:21.190
I mean, we pay homage to it!

00:20:21.190 --> 00:20:23.790
Or we can have Rame-sempai do it.

00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:25.480
That's crazy.

00:20:25.480 --> 00:20:27.040
You don't make anything for Comic 
Festival! You just buy stuff, right?

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:29.220
Then you've got time 
at the end of the year.

00:20:29.220 --> 00:20:31.700
There's no way. I don't 
know what girls like...

00:20:31.700 --> 00:20:33.170
Then at this Comic Festival...

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:34.370
Here.

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:36.080
...we can hit up all the 
girls booths and ask!

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:36.080
Thanks.

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:38.160
I want to be part of the Yoshitake Tour!

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:39.050
Yes I am!

00:20:40.410 --> 00:20:42.470
What about you, Hato-kun?

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:45.020
Oh? I'm just going to...

00:20:45.020 --> 00:20:46.450
Going to what?

00:20:46.450 --> 00:20:48.470
I'll participate, of course!

00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:49.980
All right!

00:20:49.980 --> 00:20:50.970
At this rate,

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:54.240
next year's <i>Mebaetame</i> 
will be the biggest ever!

00:20:54.240 --> 00:20:56.950
We've split up the story and art before,

00:20:56.950 --> 00:20:58.650
but never done a whole collaboration.

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:00.480
Is it really going to work?

00:21:01.430 --> 00:21:03.440
Let's do it!

00:23:30.100 --> 00:23:31.740
You came!

00:23:31.740 --> 00:23:32.900
Welcome back.

00:23:32.900 --> 00:23:34.850
We've got good pictures.

00:23:34.850 --> 00:23:35.870
So we made prints!

00:23:35.870 --> 00:23:37.100
Come take a look!

00:23:37.100 --> 00:23:40.100
<b><i>Genshiken Second Generation</i>
 The End</b>
